==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|orv|корабль}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*korabľь}}, an old borrowing from {{der|ru|grc|καράβιον}} or {{m|grc|κάραβος}}, whence English {{m|en|caravel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|кора́бль}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-{{PAGENAME}}.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|b|кора́бль|m|adj=корабе́льный|dim=кора́блик}}

# [[ship]], [[liner]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[спи́сывать]]/[[списа́ть]] [[с]] '''корабля́'''|to transfer/post from '''a ship'''}}
# {{lb|ru|formally}} [[warship]]
# {{lb|ru|architecture}} [[nave]]
# {{lb|ru|figuratively}} match box for [[marijuana]], by consonance with {{m|ru|коробок}}

====Usage notes====
* In modern technical and formal usage, корабль refers to warships. Informally, can refer to various large ships. Historically, referred to [[square-rigged]] sailing ships, similarly to the historical sense of the English word "ship".

